# Session Wrap — Changelog Workflow

After any non-trivial session (debug, fix, feature, refactor, research):

1. Evaluate what changed or was discovered
2. Commit all modified source files with a conventional commit message
3. Append an entry to `CHANGELOG.md` (create if absent) in Keep a Changelog format

**Trigger phrases (run without asking):** "wrap up", "commit findings",
"save and commit", "update changelog", "log our changes", "commit the fix".

## Project Notes

- Build & reinstall: `./script/reinstall-sidecar.sh`
- Push: `git push --no-verify origin feat/proxy`
- Active branch: `feat/proxy`

## Commit Convention

Use Conventional Commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`, `chore:`.
